<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Lugasi State</h1><p class="st-meta">1750 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Lugasi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A minor principality of the Bundelkhand Agency, one of many small holdings left from the break-up of Bundela power.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Lugasi became a separate chiefship in the mid-18th century during the fragmentation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundela</a> kingdoms, and its holder received a British sanad in the early 19th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded of its history. It was a small non-salute state of a few villages, supervised by the political agent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After independence Lugasi was merged with the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> states into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a>, and its lands were absorbed into the Indian administration by 1950.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1750 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.53%;width:3.98%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1750 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lugasi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lugasi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=lugasi-state" aria-label="Lugasi State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6684 1255 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lugasi State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7004 1511L7364 1601M7004 1511L7364 1602M7004 1511L7160 1530"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7160 1530h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7004 1511h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7004 1511h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lugasi. <a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=lugasi-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
